<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 976" role="img" aria-label="JobbyJob system architecture: where it runs, what it talks to and who may write to each store" aria-describedby="jjm-arch-desc" font-family="var(--sans)">
<title id="jjm-arch-title">JobbyJob system architecture</title>
<desc id="jjm-arch-desc">Local-first AI job search platform. External services on the left: Gmail, browser-only boards, employer application forms, job sources, Anthropic Claude and OpenAI Realtime. The local Mac runs Chrome with a browser agent and autofill extension, a Claude Code operator console and a launchd schedule; a Python ingestion pipeline that fetches, filters, judges, verifies and hands every record to a single writer; a TypeScript web app and interview coach; and local files, a knowledge vault, headless Chrome for PDFs and backups. Teable, PostgreSQL and Redis run in containers. Each store has one writer: the pipeline writer creates Teable records and reads them back, the web app writes the resume master through a versioned API, and a recorder appends score history. Knowledge graph, workflow engine and agent runtime containers are stopped by design.</desc>
